{"title":"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the parallelogram, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f72f79af3fd06c585084e93a48931f2c019961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 30 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 50 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 70 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 80 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can name the vertices to make the problem easier to understand.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Opposite angles in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">parallelogram</a> are equal, so we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/5494e5cd04cf62fd2256e73583064d4e7f792e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = m\\angle ADC = 80^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"220\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can notice that angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/4940d5d8250235d1a6478898a4b3eff8c8d630c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BFE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9e8301adfeeb2f1c3459e41d0099251907f346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CFE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> form a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">straight angle</a>, allowing us to set up an equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14536c1b796e43fd86768cf60ba23394ef9e13f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BFE + m\\angle CFE = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/4844c8a48741e646e4454b143b365e4937db9459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BFE + 150 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/669d66a2a52da5acf5682361a0a398e474484536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BFE = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can now use the fact that the angles in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> are always supplementary. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba26344ae2e227f08f1a3efe6aa292e7a2614e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + m\\angle BFE + m\\angle ABC = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"252\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88af62de3ed3763d28e8f45453ee2e6d0ffb2730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 30 + 80 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db01042902a57ec019a8e1766bc659b3d53337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 110 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/22075363d49038c231e4b5892d69d75d7c9e2c10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal\">1999 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1